From: BYTE <byte@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] qmi_wwan_q: compile the rmnet_nss hook out

qmi_wwan_q 1.5 defines CONFIG_QCA_NSS_DRV whenever the target pinctrl is
IPQ807x/IPQ5018/IPQ8074, which is the case here, and then references
rmnet_nss_callbacks from the separate rmnet_nss.ko (qmodem "rmnet-nss"
package). That module is not in this image: it depends on
+NSS_DRV_C2C_ENABLE, a chip-to-chip path that an AW1000 has no use for, so
the module is unselectable and modpost aborts with

  ERROR: modpost: "rmnet_nss_callbacks" [qmi_wwan_q.ko] undefined!

Dropping the two #define lines removes the reference. The driver keeps its
own QMAP implementation (qmap_mode/rx_qmap module params, no rmnet_data
imports), so wwan* netdevs keep working; only the optional NSS RX hand-off
goes away. ECM never accelerates wwan*/rmnet* anyway (patch 0027), so no
offload is lost on the WAN path that this firmware uses.

--- a/qmi_wwan_q.c
+++ b/qmi_wwan_q.c
@@ -58,7 +58,7 @@
 #define QMI_USBNET_HAS_BH_WORK (LINUX_VERSION_CODE >= KERNEL_VERSION(6, 17, 0))
 
 #ifdef CONFIG_PINCTRL_IPQ807x
-#define CONFIG_QCA_NSS_DRV
+/* BYTE: rmnet_nss absent, NSS hook compiled out */
 //#define CONFIG_QCA_NSS_PACKET_FILTER
 #endif
 
@@ -72,7 +72,7 @@
 static struct rmnet_nss_cb __read_mostly *nss_cb = NULL;
 #if defined(CONFIG_PINCTRL_IPQ807x) || defined(CONFIG_PINCTRL_IPQ5018) || defined(CONFIG_PINCTRL_IPQ8074)
 //#ifdef CONFIG_RMNET_DATA //spf12.x none, not effect for spf11.x
-#define CONFIG_QCA_NSS_DRV
+/* BYTE: rmnet_nss absent, NSS hook compiled out */
 /* define at qsdk/qca/src/linux-4.4/net/rmnet_data/rmnet_data_main.c */ //for spf11.x
 /* define at qsdk/qca/src/datarmnet/core/rmnet_config.c */ //for spf12.x
 /* set at qsdk/qca/src/data-kernel/drivers/rmnet-nss/rmnet_nss.c */
